    {
      "id": "claim_5496c406365e4a19a0a5cddedb9558ee",
      "statement": "The server's `bootstrap` subcommand (cmd/server/bootstrap.go) takes master database credentials via --dsn or ROSA_TA_DB_MASTER_DSN and calls store.BootstrapDatabase, which applies idempotent SQL creating the trusted_actions_app role with rds_iam and CREATEDB grants and transferring database and schema ownership to it, asserting post-conditions so a partial bootstrap fails loudly; scripts/localstack-db.sh invokes this subcommand against the LocalStack-provisioned instance using master credentials, then writes ROSA_TA_DB_* variables (no password) to .env.localstack-db for `make run-localstack-db`.",
